WEBVTT

00:00:08.750 --> 00:00:10.880
Pang Nuan, god of war.

00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:15.390
Thanks to General Biao's
going-away present,

00:00:15.390 --> 00:00:18.100
only one of those arms is of any use.

00:00:18.470 --> 00:00:19.890
And I'm gonna use

00:00:19.890 --> 00:00:22.390
all that I carry on my shoulders...

00:00:24.020 --> 00:00:27.190
It's no use! He's way out of range!

00:00:28.230 --> 00:00:31.070
No--the boy's true target...

00:00:31.070 --> 00:00:33.150
...all that I have, all that I am...

00:00:35.110 --> 00:00:36.700
...and smash you!

00:02:09.870 --> 00:02:12.460
He came after my weapon!

00:02:16.630 --> 00:02:18.170
Know thy pla--

00:02:19.550 --> 00:02:20.550
What?!

00:02:29.270 --> 00:02:30.270
"Wei"

00:02:46.370 --> 00:02:47.660
Xin!

00:02:47.660 --> 00:02:49.040
Pang Nuan--

00:02:49.040 --> 00:02:50.870
He knocked Pang Nuan away!

00:03:00.840 --> 00:03:02.090
<i>Still </i>not done?

00:03:02.090 --> 00:03:03.350
You ain't runnin'!

00:03:04.800 --> 00:03:06.310
Hi-His leg!

00:03:46.180 --> 00:03:47.180
Xin...

00:03:57.270 --> 00:03:58.400
Li Mu.

00:03:58.940 --> 00:04:00.690
Jin Chengchang.

00:04:00.690 --> 00:04:03.360
"Zhao"

00:04:00.690 --> 00:04:03.360
Why are you hesitating?

00:04:03.360 --> 00:04:07.200
Surely you would have realized long ago:

00:04:07.200 --> 00:04:11.580
This war is decided--
however unfortunate the result.

00:04:19.800 --> 00:04:21.050
I am aware.

00:04:22.510 --> 00:04:26.550
Pull out all but the south army.

00:04:26.550 --> 00:04:29.930
The south army will buy
us time bringing up the rear.

00:04:29.930 --> 00:04:32.730
Then... you mean...

00:04:32.730 --> 00:04:35.310
All troops... are to withdraw.

00:04:39.070 --> 00:04:42.900
I'll stay behind with the south
army and fulfill my responsibilities.

00:04:42.900 --> 00:04:44.200
You will not.

00:04:44.200 --> 00:04:48.530
The one person who absolutely
must not lose their life in this place

00:04:48.530 --> 00:04:52.790
is one of those responsible for this war:

00:04:52.790 --> 00:04:54.250
you, Li Mu.

00:04:54.250 --> 00:04:58.790
You have a duty to find a point of
compromise for the coalition army.

00:05:01.250 --> 00:05:06.510
No matter the outcome, Li Mu,
you must see it through to the end.

00:05:06.510 --> 00:05:07.930
Jin Chengchang...

00:05:09.100 --> 00:05:10.390
I am most grateful.

00:05:10.390 --> 00:05:15.850
Don't mention it. Bringing up
the rear is an old man's job.

00:05:15.850 --> 00:05:17.650
But you know...

00:05:17.650 --> 00:05:22.070
The great general Pang Nuan
needs to retreat as well.

00:05:22.070 --> 00:05:25.200
What to do, what to do...

00:05:29.620 --> 00:05:30.990
Pang Nuan will--

00:05:35.040 --> 00:05:36.040
Xin!

00:05:38.960 --> 00:05:40.670
This cannot be.

00:05:40.670 --> 00:05:43.460
Such a deep wound,
from such a young whelp...

00:05:44.760 --> 00:05:47.880
Why was I outmatched to start?

00:05:49.390 --> 00:05:51.930
The impossible has happened.

00:05:54.890 --> 00:05:56.600
What are you?

00:05:56.600 --> 00:05:59.850
What <i>are </i>you lot?!

00:06:05.530 --> 00:06:08.780
Pang Nuan, sir! Please withdraw!

00:06:08.780 --> 00:06:10.700
Pang Nuan.

00:06:10.700 --> 00:06:13.950
Quietly, now, reconsider where you stand.

00:06:14.540 --> 00:06:18.210
You'll find the answer
has already revealed itself.

00:06:18.210 --> 00:06:20.880
There you are, in darkness,

00:06:20.880 --> 00:06:23.590
standing where your path ends.

00:06:27.840 --> 00:06:29.180
Oh, and--

00:06:29.180 --> 00:06:31.140
These are Li Mu's words, of course.

00:06:32.640 --> 00:06:37.350
Where my path ends?

00:06:37.350 --> 00:06:39.810
Please withdraw, Pang Nuan, sir.

00:06:39.810 --> 00:06:43.520
All our armies are in retreat.

00:06:43.520 --> 00:06:49.030
No one who remains here
alone will live--not even you.

00:06:49.030 --> 00:06:54.370
Falling halfway along your path
is hardly your ambition, I'm sure.

00:06:54.370 --> 00:06:58.250
Did... did he just say... "in retreat"?

00:07:09.470 --> 00:07:12.010
I shall let this go--once.

00:07:14.050 --> 00:07:15.430
However...

00:07:15.430 --> 00:07:18.930
...I will <i>not </i>forget thy name...

00:07:18.930 --> 00:07:19.930
...Xin.

00:07:28.860 --> 00:07:29.940
It...

00:07:29.940 --> 00:07:31.400
It worked.

00:07:31.400 --> 00:07:34.240
Thank goodness... Pang Nuan...

00:07:35.660 --> 00:07:39.410
He drove off Pang Nuan!

00:07:41.620 --> 00:07:43.120
Wait...

00:07:43.120 --> 00:07:44.210
Pang Nuan!

00:07:46.710 --> 00:07:48.130
Whoa! Xin!

00:07:49.550 --> 00:07:54.050
I believe that man is the scourge of Qin.
Shall we go after him?

00:07:54.050 --> 00:07:55.800
How could we not?

00:07:55.800 --> 00:07:57.350
Hang in there, Xin!

00:07:59.850 --> 00:08:02.350
The mountain folk--
they're after Pang Nuan!

00:08:02.350 --> 00:08:03.770
Go get 'im!

00:08:06.440 --> 00:08:08.570
Yip yip! Yip yip!

00:08:08.570 --> 00:08:11.780
You wretched mountain monkeys!
Unforgivable!

00:08:11.780 --> 00:08:16.320
Don't you understand?
Thanks to you rank outsiders,

00:08:16.320 --> 00:08:21.960
the very history of the Middle Kingdom
itself has been twisted!

00:08:25.880 --> 00:08:28.420
Of <i>course </i>we understand.

00:08:28.420 --> 00:08:33.130
But this is hardly impulsive meddling.

00:08:33.130 --> 00:08:37.800
This stems from an alliance
with Qin's Duke Mu 400 years ago--

00:08:37.800 --> 00:08:43.640
and one I, Yang Duanhe,
now share with their current King.

00:08:43.640 --> 00:08:44.980
Th-That's ridiculous--

00:08:44.980 --> 00:08:49.570
Enough of your chattering,
you old flatlander general.

00:08:49.570 --> 00:08:54.320
Be silent, and let your names go down
in history as the losers you are.

00:08:56.820 --> 00:09:01.080
Y-You <i>ape</i>! How dare you
speak the human tongue?!

00:09:01.080 --> 00:09:03.000
Kill them all!

00:09:59.010 --> 00:10:01.890
The conclusion of the battle at Zui

00:10:01.890 --> 00:10:03.970
appeared in the "House of Zhao"
chapter of Historical Records,

00:10:03.970 --> 00:10:05.890
a brief mention in a single sentence.

00:10:07.140 --> 00:10:10.310
"In the year 241 BC,

00:10:10.310 --> 00:10:16.700
Pang Nuan led elite troops
from Zhao, Chu, Wei, and Yan

00:10:16.700 --> 00:10:19.030
in a siege of Zui in Qin...

00:10:25.830 --> 00:10:28.000
...but failed."

00:10:28.420 --> 00:10:33.040
"Qin"

00:10:38.050 --> 00:10:42.050
"Xianyang"

00:10:47.060 --> 00:10:50.150
Could... could you repeat that?

00:10:50.150 --> 00:10:52.440
Y-Yes, sir!

00:10:52.440 --> 00:10:55.360
The Li Mu Army has retreated from Zui!

00:10:55.360 --> 00:10:57.490
All armies have withdrawn!

00:11:04.990 --> 00:11:06.200
We did it!

00:11:06.200 --> 00:11:07.750
Well done!

00:11:07.750 --> 00:11:09.210
Hooray!

00:11:29.180 --> 00:11:31.730
Xiang--oh, Xiang!

00:11:36.070 --> 00:11:39.530
"Zui"

00:11:49.700 --> 00:11:52.170
Yang Duanhe.

00:11:52.170 --> 00:11:55.790
Good job holding out so long, Ying Zheng.

00:11:55.790 --> 00:11:58.340
I'm just glad we made it in time.

00:12:04.220 --> 00:12:05.220
Thank you.

00:12:06.930 --> 00:12:09.560
You saved us--truly.

00:12:10.560 --> 00:12:11.560
Thank you.

00:12:24.110 --> 00:12:25.490
Ow, ow, ow...

00:12:32.540 --> 00:12:33.870
We did it.

00:12:35.460 --> 00:12:36.460
Yes.

00:12:42.970 --> 00:12:45.220
That Long Chuan sure is noisy.

00:12:46.720 --> 00:12:49.390
It's no good, Tian Yǒu, sir.

00:12:49.390 --> 00:12:51.520
Right now, Ji Rong and Jue...

00:12:53.060 --> 00:12:54.060
Understood.

00:12:56.860 --> 00:12:58.520
He Liao Diao! How's Xin?

00:12:58.520 --> 00:13:00.480
Is Xin okay?!

00:13:00.480 --> 00:13:03.820
He's fine. Sleeping like a log.

00:13:03.820 --> 00:13:07.410
I expect he'll be down for the
count for another two, three days.

00:13:08.120 --> 00:13:11.750
Really? Well, at least he's all right.

00:13:11.750 --> 00:13:16.120
I gotta say, Xin really
took me by surprise.

00:13:16.120 --> 00:13:19.130
I mean, driving back Pang Nuan like that?

00:13:19.130 --> 00:13:20.130
Yeah.

00:13:21.960 --> 00:13:27.180
When he said he was heading down there,
I took him for a stone-cold moron.

00:13:27.180 --> 00:13:31.510
But when I saw him fighting...
how can I put this...

00:13:32.770 --> 00:13:35.190
I was proud.

00:13:36.140 --> 00:13:39.940
When I saw Xin fighting Pang Nuan,

00:13:41.230 --> 00:13:43.860
I thought how lucky I was

00:13:43.860 --> 00:13:47.660
to be part of the Fei Xin Force--
part of <i>his </i>unit.

00:13:56.290 --> 00:13:57.460
Me, too.

00:14:01.040 --> 00:14:02.750
Even if he <i>is </i>an idiot.

00:14:02.750 --> 00:14:03.760
Right?

00:14:17.060 --> 00:14:19.270
Ow! Ow, ow, ow...

00:14:39.500 --> 00:14:41.210
Ain't even dawn yet...

00:14:42.040 --> 00:14:43.750
Everybody's asleep.

00:14:59.770 --> 00:15:00.770
Xin!

00:15:01.900 --> 00:15:03.060
Hey.

00:15:03.060 --> 00:15:04.230
Ow, ow, ow...

00:15:10.280 --> 00:15:11.950
It's all over now.

00:15:11.950 --> 00:15:13.410
Right, Zheng?

00:15:14.950 --> 00:15:17.330
Most certainly.

00:15:17.330 --> 00:15:22.790
Li Mu's detached force was
the coalition army's last resort.

00:15:22.790 --> 00:15:26.130
Since we continue to supply
our troops at Hangu Pass,

00:15:26.130 --> 00:15:29.550
they won't be breaching that, either.

00:15:29.550 --> 00:15:31.470
Good.

00:15:31.470 --> 00:15:36.140
Man, those mountain-folk reinforcements
came in the nick of time, eh?

00:15:36.140 --> 00:15:38.770
I get goosebumps now
just thinkin' about it.

00:15:41.310 --> 00:15:43.440
But what was <i>really </i>amazin'...

00:15:45.940 --> 00:15:50.650
...was the civilians holdin' Zui together,
right down to their breakin' points.

00:15:50.650 --> 00:15:52.700
Yes.

00:15:52.700 --> 00:15:56.530
For people who were gonna
surrender to Li Mu's army,

00:15:56.530 --> 00:16:00.460
they sure responded to what you
told 'em--and fought on through.

00:16:01.870 --> 00:16:02.960
Right, Zheng?

00:16:07.130 --> 00:16:09.920
According to last night's report,

00:16:09.920 --> 00:16:14.840
half of Zui lost their lives
over these past seven days.

00:16:21.100 --> 00:16:22.480
I see.

00:16:22.480 --> 00:16:26.900
But their sacrifice is what kept
Zui from bein' conquered.

00:16:27.360 --> 00:16:29.110
Qin was saved!

00:16:29.110 --> 00:16:32.070
They didn't die in vain.

00:16:32.070 --> 00:16:33.740
Indeed.

00:16:33.740 --> 00:16:35.120
Still,

00:16:35.120 --> 00:16:39.580
as the instigator who egged them on,
resulting in 10,000 dead,

00:16:39.580 --> 00:16:42.580
something is piercing
me deep within my chest.

00:16:44.370 --> 00:16:45.880
Zheng...

00:16:45.880 --> 00:16:47.500
I...

00:16:47.500 --> 00:16:53.010
I came to Zui thinking the King's
words might turn them toward battle.

00:16:54.090 --> 00:16:59.930
Inciting them with clever patter
to fight to their dying breath--

00:16:59.930 --> 00:17:04.520
in one sense, it's worse
than drafting them by force.

00:17:04.520 --> 00:17:06.310
You gotta stop that, Zheng.

00:17:06.310 --> 00:17:08.270
I understand how you feel,

00:17:08.270 --> 00:17:10.860
but you did what you could do.

00:17:15.740 --> 00:17:19.330
Apologies. I'm whining a bit.

00:17:21.830 --> 00:17:23.830
They're such different things--

00:17:25.710 --> 00:17:29.420
war as we know it from
reports at the Royal Court

00:17:29.420 --> 00:17:32.960
and war as it happens
right before one's eyes.

00:17:32.960 --> 00:17:34.550
'Course they are.

00:17:34.550 --> 00:17:38.430
If it don't make you feel something,
you ain't right in the head.

00:17:38.430 --> 00:17:42.310
And you sure as <i>hell </i>ain't
fit to lead anyone else.

00:17:45.140 --> 00:17:48.980
I'm sure you did come
here thinkin' what you did.

00:17:50.820 --> 00:17:52.780
But y'know, Zheng...

00:17:52.780 --> 00:17:55.740
Along the way, I started thinkin':

00:17:55.740 --> 00:17:57.820
The people of Zui ain't stupid.

00:17:57.820 --> 00:18:01.330
They probably knew they
were bein' taken for a ride.

00:18:02.830 --> 00:18:04.750
And even knowin' as much,

00:18:04.750 --> 00:18:08.670
they <i>still </i>fought till the
very end, eyes all a-glitter.

00:18:19.260 --> 00:18:20.890
You are exactly right.

00:18:23.060 --> 00:18:26.430
Qin would have perished without them.

00:18:40.030 --> 00:18:41.030
Zheng...

00:18:53.340 --> 00:18:55.800
Are you really leaving so soon?

00:18:55.800 --> 00:18:58.880
Yes. Back to battling
the Pangu in the north.

00:19:01.850 --> 00:19:05.810
Let's meet again once things settle
down for both of us, Yang Duanhe.

00:19:05.810 --> 00:19:06.810
Let's.

00:19:12.560 --> 00:19:13.520
All right!

00:19:14.820 --> 00:19:16.740
Let us return--to Xianyang!

00:19:21.200 --> 00:19:23.490
Four days later,

00:19:23.490 --> 00:19:27.750
Li Mu and his army finally
returned to Hangu Pass

00:19:27.750 --> 00:19:29.960
"Yan" "Wei" "Chu" "Zhao" "Han"

00:19:27.750 --> 00:19:29.960
and joined up with the coalition army.

00:19:31.580 --> 00:19:33.080
Oh?

00:19:33.080 --> 00:19:38.210
Fat lot of nerve this loser of
a general has, coming back alive.

00:19:41.130 --> 00:19:44.930
That's what Zhang Yin
of Han said. Earlier.

00:19:44.930 --> 00:19:45.930
Huh?!

00:19:47.850 --> 00:19:49.730
Before I die,

00:19:49.730 --> 00:19:54.440
I must decide where the blade
I've raised will land.

00:19:54.440 --> 00:19:58.820
When Qin took Shanyang,
key stronghold of the Middle Kingdom,

00:19:58.820 --> 00:20:01.910
I began forming a coalition army.

00:20:01.910 --> 00:20:04.660
Let us at least return Shanyang to Wei--

00:20:04.660 --> 00:20:05.660
Mediocre!

00:20:07.450 --> 00:20:12.920
Taking back the likes of Shanyang
will hardly satisfy us now.

00:20:12.920 --> 00:20:16.090
Our next target has already been decided.

00:20:17.750 --> 00:20:21.590
This coalition army has had
a traitor in its midst all along.

00:20:26.810 --> 00:20:27.970
You don't mean...

00:20:29.020 --> 00:20:31.430
All armies, move out!

00:20:31.430 --> 00:20:34.400
"Yan" "Wei" "Chu" "Zhao" "Han"

00:20:31.430 --> 00:20:34.400
Our battle is not yet over!

00:20:36.940 --> 00:20:38.570
L-Look at that!

00:20:41.280 --> 00:20:42.950
"Meng"

00:20:41.280 --> 00:20:42.950
The enemy...

00:20:42.950 --> 00:20:45.530
The coalition army is retreating!

00:20:45.530 --> 00:20:48.660
--Hooray!
--We did it!

00:20:48.660 --> 00:20:51.290
Ha-Hangu Pass stands firm!

00:20:59.500 --> 00:21:01.880
We did it, Zhang Tang.

00:21:03.840 --> 00:21:06.260
Serves you right!

00:21:06.260 --> 00:21:08.140
What's got your goat?

00:21:09.220 --> 00:21:10.810
Oh, nothing.

00:21:10.810 --> 00:21:12.390
It's just, you know...

00:21:12.390 --> 00:21:15.350
...defense is such a bore.

00:21:23.240 --> 00:21:26.990
I'm glad Lu Wuwei and
the others didn't die in vain.

00:21:26.990 --> 00:21:27.990
Hey!

00:21:33.660 --> 00:21:37.710
M-Meng Tian--he's d--

00:21:37.710 --> 00:21:39.340
He's dead...

00:21:39.340 --> 00:21:41.500
...asleep!

00:21:41.500 --> 00:21:44.050
Please, adjutant--you'll jinx him!

00:21:44.050 --> 00:21:45.260
Meng Tian, sir!

00:21:46.130 --> 00:21:48.300
Sir? It's over.

00:21:51.930 --> 00:21:54.100
Just my luck.

00:21:54.100 --> 00:21:57.440
I never did run across an enemy general
whose head was worth taking.

00:22:01.360 --> 00:22:04.530
The coalition army,
having failed to conquer Qin,

00:22:04.530 --> 00:22:06.740
reversed course

00:22:06.740 --> 00:22:08.570
"Qin" "Qi"

00:22:06.740 --> 00:22:08.570
and attacked Qi.

00:22:09.320 --> 00:22:11.790
"Chu"

00:22:12.240 --> 00:22:16.290
Report! The castles of Bing
and Cao have fallen!

00:22:16.670 --> 00:22:21.710
"King of Qi" "Wang Jian"
Ah, the greediness of Li Mu--
no, Lord Chunshen.

00:22:21.710 --> 00:22:24.340
Trying to snatch from
Qi the land and riches

00:22:24.340 --> 00:22:27.180
you'd expected to steal from Qin, eh?

00:22:29.180 --> 00:22:33.720
Then it's all-out war between
Qi and the coalition army.

00:22:33.720 --> 00:22:35.180
Urgent report!

00:22:35.180 --> 00:22:36.730
It--it's Meng Wu!

00:22:39.730 --> 00:22:44.780
Qin general Meng Wu's army is
attacking the coalition army's back!

00:22:44.780 --> 00:22:46.780
They're <i>what</i>?!

00:22:48.070 --> 00:22:49.070
Oho!

00:22:50.160 --> 00:22:53.830
That's Lord Changping for you.
He wastes no time.

00:22:56.410 --> 00:23:00.080
Despite the unexpected rear attack,

00:23:00.080 --> 00:23:03.000
the coalition army conquered
Qi's capital, Rao'an,

00:23:03.000 --> 00:23:04.420
where, at last,

00:23:04.420 --> 00:23:06.210
they disbanded.

00:23:08.380 --> 00:23:12.470
Thus the battle between Qin and the
coalition army, lasting over a month,

00:23:12.470 --> 00:23:15.640
was brought to a close.

00:23:18.810 --> 00:23:21.980
"Deepest Gratitude"

00:24:54.280 --> 00:24:57.990
Next on <i>Kingdom</i>:
"The Difference Between Dances."
